# Store every text file as LF in the repository and check every text file out as
# LF, no matter what core.autocrlf says on the contributor's machine.
#
# Without this, the repo silently depends on everyone having autocrlf=true. Edit
# index.html from Linux, macOS, or a Windows box with autocrlf=false and git
# sees all 2,661 lines as rewritten — a diff full of phantom changes that can get
# committed and served to GitHub Pages.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, declared explicitly so line-ending conversion can never touch
# them regardless of what auto-detection decides.
*.jpg  binary
*.avif binary
*.xlsx binary
